# L §4.4 / §5.18: "windows each prints one line per maximal sub-window, or combination of sub-windows, over which
# the answer is constant, and one plain line when the answer doesn't depend on the day".  d is any day of 07-01 ..
# 07-10: d < 07-05 is true on 07-01 .. 07-04 and false on 07-05 .. 07-10; d == d doesn't depend on the day.  Two
# windows (d1 in 07-01..07-03, d2 in 07-02..07-04), d1 < d2: true where d1 < d2.  Lines: this interpreter's layout
# `<ask> [<window> = <days>]`, boxes of consecutive days taken in day order (the cover of the second ask is not
# unique: reported).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

input d: date
input d1: date
input d2: date
input cutoff: date

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  d = window(2020-07-01, 2020-07-10)
  d1 = window(2020-07-01, 2020-07-03)
  d2 = window(2020-07-02, 2020-07-04)
  cutoff = 2020-07-05

ask q1: d < cutoff windows each
ask q2: d == d windows each
ask q3: d1 < d2 windows each
=== expect
q1 [d = 2020-07-01 .. 2020-07-04]: true
  cut 2026-12-31
q1 [d = 2020-07-05 .. 2020-07-10]: false
  cut 2026-12-31
q2: true
  cut 2026-12-31
q3 [d1 = 2020-07-01, d2 = 2020-07-02 .. 2020-07-04]: true
  cut 2026-12-31
q3 [d1 = 2020-07-02 .. 2020-07-03, d2 = 2020-07-02]: false
  cut 2026-12-31
q3 [d1 = 2020-07-02, d2 = 2020-07-03 .. 2020-07-04]: true
  cut 2026-12-31
q3 [d1 = 2020-07-03, d2 = 2020-07-03]: false
  cut 2026-12-31
q3 [d1 = 2020-07-03, d2 = 2020-07-04]: true
  cut 2026-12-31
